251 |   def kbet(rep: np.ndarray, groups: np.ndarray, k: int = 20) -> float:
252 | /     """kBET acceptance rate (Büttner et al., 2019) — chi-squared per-cell test.
253 | |
254 | |     For each cell, compares the observed group frequency in its k-NN
255 | |     neighbourhood to the global expected frequency via a chi-squared
256 | |     statistic, then returns the **fraction of cells whose neighbourhood does
257 | |     not reject H0 at alpha=0.05** (i.e. is well-mixed).
258 | |
259 | |     A *higher* acceptance rate means better mixing.
260 | |
261 | |     .. note::
262 | |         The previous implementation returned ``exp(-mean_chi2)`` which is
263 | |         a monotone transformation, not the chi-squared acceptance rate.
264 | |
265 | |     Parameters
266 | |     ----------
267 | |     rep:
268 | |         2-D array of shape ``(n_cells, n_dims)``.
269 | |     groups:
270 | |         1-D array of group labels, length ``n_cells``.
271 | |     k:
272 | |         Neighbourhood size.
273 | |
274 | |     Returns
275 | |     -------
276 | |     float
277 | |         kBET acceptance rate in [0, 1]. **Higher = better mixing.**
278 | |     """
