551 |   ) -> pd.DataFrame:
552 | /     """Per-dimension activity statistics for a latent matrix.
553 | |
554 | |     Computes the standard deviation and mean absolute value of each column.
555 | |     When ``mu_array`` and ``sigma_array`` are provided (posterior mean and
556 | |     standard deviation), uses the **per-dimension marginal KL** against
557 | |     N(0, 1) to flag collapsed dimensions (W-052):
558 | |
559 | |     .. math::
560 | |         \\text{KL}_d = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_i \\left[
561 | |             \\frac{\\mu_{i,d}^2 + \\sigma_{i,d}^2}{2}
562 | |             - \\log \\sigma_{i,d} - \\frac{1}{2}
563 | |         \\right]
564 | |
565 | |     A dimension is flagged ``is_collapsed`` when its mean KL < ``threshold``
566 | |     (default 0.05, following Bowman et al. and the standard VAE collapse
567 | |     literature). When only the sample array is provided, falls back to the
568 | |     std-heuristic with the same ``threshold``.
569 | |
570 | |     Parameters
571 | |     ----------
572 | |     latent_array:
573 | |         2-D array of shape ``(n_cells, n_dims)``.
574 | |     mu_array:
575 | |         Optional posterior mean array, same shape as ``latent_array``.
576 | |     sigma_array:
577 | |         Optional posterior std array, same shape as ``latent_array``.
578 | |     threshold:
579 | |         KL threshold below which a dimension is flagged as collapsed
580 | |         (when mu/sigma provided), or std threshold (fallback).
581 | |
582 | |     Returns
583 | |     -------
584 | |     pd.DataFrame
585 | |         One row per dimension. Columns:
586 | |
587 | |         ``dim``
588 | |             Dimension index.
589 | |         ``std``
590 | |             Population standard deviation of z across cells.
591 | |         ``mean_abs``
592 | |             Mean absolute value of z across cells.
593 | |         ``mean_kl``
594 | |             Per-dimension mean KL against N(0, 1). ``nan`` if mu/sigma
595 | |             not provided.
596 | |         ``is_collapsed``
597 | |             ``True`` if the dimension is deemed collapsed.
598 | |         ``rank``
599 | |             Rank by std (1 = most active).
600 | |
601 | |     Examples
602 | |     --------
603 | |     >>> stats = spVIPESmulti.metrics.latent_dimension_stats(z_shared)
604 | |     >>> print(stats[stats.is_collapsed])
605 | |     """
